From: UTDeck
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: ask again for fullscreen when the compositor takes it away

Lomiri (Ubuntu Touch) grants a new window's fullscreen request and then, once the window has drawn,
gives it the state its app's last window closed in: a normal window under the top panel (stage
4.1, traced on Ys: Memories of Celceta: 1080x2400 fullscreen, then 1080x2400 and 2400x1017
normal). The Win32 window stays fullscreen-sized, nothing in it changes afterwards, and so nothing
asks again. Patch 0004's check (on each presented frame, 0.5 s after the last configure, at most
three times) now also asks when the compositor's state is not fullscreen at all, once the window
has been configured and no configure waits.
---

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -489,7 +489,8 @@
  * fullscreen. Like the Dolphin port of Ubuntu Touch: once the size has been stable for 0.5 s (a
  * rotation passes through intermediate sizes), if the fullscreen window does not cover the output,
  * ask for fullscreen again (unset, then set), at most three times; the count is reset once the
- * window covers the output. Called with the window data locked, when a frame is presented. */
+ * window covers the output. The same when the compositor has taken fullscreen away altogether.
+ * Called with the window data locked, when a frame is presented. */
 void wayland_surface_check_fullscreen_size(struct wayland_surface *surface)
 {
     struct wayland_output *output;
@@ -497,12 +498,30 @@
     int height = surface->current.rect.bottom - surface->current.rect.top;
     int out_w = 0, out_h = 0;
 
-    if (!(surface->current.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN) ||
-        !(surface->window.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN) ||
-        !width || !height || !surface->xdg_toplevel ||
+    /* Not before the first configure, nor while one waits to be applied. */
+    if (!(surface->window.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN) ||
+        !surface->xdg_toplevel || !surface->current.serial || surface->requested.serial ||
         (int)(NtGetTickCount() - surface->fullscreen_check_time) < 0)
         return;
 
+    /* UTDeck: the compositor took fullscreen away while the window still wants it (it still
+     * covers its monitor). Lomiri grants a new window's fullscreen request and then gives the
+     * window the state its app's last window closed in, once it has drawn: a normal window under
+     * the top panel. Nothing in the window changes afterwards, so nothing would ask again. Ask once
+     * the state has been settled for 0.5 s, at most three times. */
+    if (!(surface->current.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN))
+    {
+        if (surface->fullscreen_retries >= 3) return;
+        surface->fullscreen_retries++;
+        surface->fullscreen_check_time = NtGetTickCount() + 500;
+        TRACE("hwnd=%p fullscreen was taken away, asking again (%d)\n",
+              surface->hwnd, surface->fullscreen_retries);
+        xdg_toplevel_set_fullscreen(surface->xdg_toplevel, NULL);
+        wl_display_flush(process_wayland.wl_display);
+        return;
+    }
+    if (!width || !height) return;
+
     pthread_mutex_lock(&process_wayland.output_mutex);
     wl_list_for_each(output, &process_wayland.output_list, link)
     {
